WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:02.070
- Honorary Oscar to anyone.

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:03.053
Hmm.

00:00:03.053 --> 00:00:05.636
(bright music)

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:10.800
- I would give an honorary
Oscar to Ruth Gordon,

00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:13.080
the actress in "Rosemary's Baby,"

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:15.810
the most phenomenal
performer of her generation.

00:00:15.810 --> 00:00:16.643
- Winona Ryder.

00:00:16.643 --> 00:00:17.880
I love Winona as a person,

00:00:17.880 --> 00:00:20.160
and also she's been in
so many iconic films.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.000
She means a lot to me.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.440
- Angela Bassett has done some
incredible phenomenal work

00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:26.340
as an actor.

00:00:26.340 --> 00:00:28.140
She's part of the reason
why I want to act.

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:29.760
I just want her to have that moment.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:33.210
- An actress who actually
opened a lot of doors

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:35.880
for other black actresses in the UK,

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:37.440
and her name is Carmen Munroe.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.150
I just sort of feel
like I wouldn't be here

00:00:39.150 --> 00:00:40.500
if she wasn't there.

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:42.540
- A drama teacher called Hillary Wood

00:00:42.540 --> 00:00:43.860
who trained actors at RADA

00:00:43.860 --> 00:00:45.300
and the Lir Academy where I went to.

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:47.400
I feel very grateful to
be one of her pupils.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.580
- To my high school English
teacher, a guy named Crag Hill.

00:00:50.580 --> 00:00:51.990
I don't know if I would've kept writing

00:00:51.990 --> 00:00:52.823
if it weren't for him.

00:00:52.823 --> 00:00:54.840
- I'd give an honorary Oscar to Zelensky.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:55.740
- I'm not gonna beat that.

00:00:55.740 --> 00:00:56.573
- [Carey] What a hero.

00:00:56.573 --> 00:00:57.406
And he's an actor.

00:00:57.406 --> 00:00:58.770
- [Zoe] There's a humanitarian award.

00:00:58.770 --> 00:01:00.420
Yeah, so that's him, Zelensky.

00:01:00.420 --> 00:01:01.380
- Honestly, my wife.

00:01:01.380 --> 00:01:04.620
How could I tell her how
much I appreciate her?

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:07.290
- I would think of
someone who's been working

00:01:07.290 --> 00:01:08.220
for a long time.

00:01:08.220 --> 00:01:10.260
I would have given an Oscar to my parents.

00:01:10.260 --> 00:01:11.190
- I'm just keeping it a hundred.

00:01:11.190 --> 00:01:12.150
I'd give it to my momma.

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:14.670
My brother Edwin and I,
we started in this game

00:01:14.670 --> 00:01:16.380
when we were both three years old,

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:17.520
and Mom is the one who pushed it.

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:20.739
If ever there is a day
that I ever receive,

00:01:20.739 --> 00:01:23.700
you know, an Oscar, I
would definitely dedicate

00:01:23.700 --> 00:01:25.080
and actually give that to her

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:26.610
because she deserves it the most.

00:01:26.610 --> 00:01:29.910
- I would give an honorary
Oscar to John Waters.

00:01:29.910 --> 00:01:31.440
- [Luke] That's a really good answer.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:32.520
- He really deserves one.

00:01:32.520 --> 00:01:33.660
- For her future work,

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:36.780
which I have no doubt will
be incredible, Sarah Polley.

00:01:36.780 --> 00:01:37.613
Maybe she'll get an Oscar of her own.

00:01:37.613 --> 00:01:38.682
- [Billy] I think she's
gonna get an Oscar Oscar.

00:01:38.682 --> 00:01:39.690
- [Luke] She's getting
an Oscar of her own.

00:01:39.690 --> 00:01:41.370
- Christine Vachon for
everything she's done

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:44.670
for American Independent
Film and New York Film

00:01:44.670 --> 00:01:45.510
and queer film.

00:01:45.510 --> 00:01:47.220
- David Fincher, Michael Mann,

00:01:47.220 --> 00:01:51.090
because they're iconic American filmmakers

00:01:51.090 --> 00:01:54.960
who have completely set
the tone of amazing movies.

00:01:54.960 --> 00:01:57.630
- If I could give an
honorary Oscar to someone,

00:01:57.630 --> 00:01:59.296
it would be to David Lynch.

00:01:59.296 --> 00:02:00.387
- [Interpreter] Randa Haines.

00:02:00.387 --> 00:02:02.610
She directed my first film.

00:02:02.610 --> 00:02:05.070
She was the first woman to direct a film

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:06.840
that was nominated for an Oscar.

00:02:06.840 --> 00:02:10.620
- I always feel that Ozu
deserves an honorary Oscar

00:02:10.620 --> 00:02:13.350
because his films are
so beautiful and elegant

00:02:13.350 --> 00:02:15.570
and so different from Western Cinema.

00:02:15.570 --> 00:02:18.600
- Athol Fugard, the great
South African playwright,

00:02:18.600 --> 00:02:22.770
who also, many of his plays
were made into very great films,

00:02:22.770 --> 00:02:24.660
some of which he directed himself.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:25.493
- Athol Fugard.

00:02:25.493 --> 00:02:28.440
He's just this complete
underrated, brilliant

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:31.920
Tony Award-winning,
Telluride-celebrated living artist,

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:32.910
and I think it's his time.

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:34.770
- If I could give an honorary Oscar,

00:02:34.770 --> 00:02:36.120
I would give it to the crew.

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:37.380
There are a lot of people who are there

00:02:37.380 --> 00:02:38.760
before we get to work

00:02:38.760 --> 00:02:40.440
and who stay there after we get to work

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:43.410
and who make it possible for
us to do the very best work

00:02:43.410 --> 00:02:44.760
that we are capable of doing.

00:02:44.760 --> 00:02:47.220
I wish we had more
opportunities to thank the crew.

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:49.251
- I personally would
give an honorary Oscar

00:02:49.251 --> 00:02:53.490
to all the public who
are returning post-COVID

00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:54.870
to movie theaters

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:57.210
and making movie theaters the experience

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.380
we all want 'em to be.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:00.090
So that's millions of Oscars,

00:03:00.090 --> 00:03:02.000
but I think every one of them deserves it.

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.583
(bright music)

